# Request the planner to run and return a path
# Since the global planner solution is almost deterministic,
# we could choose which frontier (using its id) from the best one to execute.
# By default, id 0 means selecting the best one.
int32 id
# Don't check for frontier properties (e.g. leaf vertex, gain, ...)
# This could be used to find a path to any vertex in the graph
bool not_check_frontier
# Force the planner to provide the path regardless the time budget.
bool ignore_time
# ROS 2 extension: collision-body mode for this global route (default: exact size).
int32 bound_mode 3
# ROS 2 extension: delayed handoff from PlanAhead's automatic frontier switch.
# Retain the selected target across interrupted local requests. Manual global
# requests leave this false; this mode requires id=0 and frontier checking.
bool automatic_repositioning
---
# Return best path.
geometry_msgs/Pose[] path
# ROS 2 extension: the zero-frontier policy returned a homing route. The PCI
# must end automatic exploration after it, even though this is a global call.
bool homing
